    "summary": "My name is Anand Khatri, from Bharatpur Raj and I'm a Mechanical Engineer with more than four years of experience in pipeline and chemical industries. Currently, I'm working as an Executive - Plant Engineering at Asian Paints Limited(top automated plant), where I manage mechanical breakdown analysis, preventive maintenance planning, and optimization of critical equipment like dispersers, mixers, pumps, and I also have a knowledge of Distributed control system and Sap mm.\n\nIn my role, I've successfully implemented cost-saving techniques, improved equipment effectiveness, and led cross-functional teams to enhance plant safety and productivity. Before this, I worked at BKT Tires, where I gained hands-on experience in machine commissioning, product trials, and quality assurance in tire manufacturing.\n\nI hold a B-Tech in Mechanical Engineering and am pursuing an Advanced Diploma in Industrial Safety, which complements my technical expertise with strong safety management skills. Along the way, I've been recognized with awards such as the Abhinandan Award and ICON of the Quarter for my contributions to breakdown reduction and safety improvements.\n\nI see myself as adaptable, analytical, and a strong team player. I'm excited about opportunities where I can apply my technical knowledge, leadership skills, and problem-solving abilities to drive efficiency, safety, and innovation in engineering operations. My short-term goal is to work with reputed organisation where I use my mentioned skills and long-term goal is to achieve a senior managerial position in a reputed organisation where I focus on my personal and organisational growth."
